# Family A9: statistics counter layouts (internal/stats). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/stats
BENCH=BenchmarkStats
REF=atomic
AUTO_KEY=stats
ADR=17
TITLE="Stats counters (A9)"
# Full profile: IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX=full sweeps P=1,8,32,64 goroutines (spec §9 A9).

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="ns/op at contention -> striped"
# MATRIX=full because §9.1's benchmark column is "contended increment at
# 8/32/64 goroutines" and the smoke grid stops at 8: the 32- and 64-goroutine
# points ARE the contention the criterion is read at, and a single atomic
# counter beats a striped one at P=1 and P=8. 36 rows, twelve minutes.
MATRIX=full
DECIDED_AT="P=1 P=8 P=32 P=64 op=add op=addat op=load"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op"
